From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:09:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] CMakeLists.txt: drop the removed app/boilerplate.cmake include

Zephyr 4.5 deletes cmake/app/boilerplate.cmake (upstream 28e363fc69c), so the
include fails the configure step:

  CMake Error at CMakeLists.txt:8 (include):
    include could not find requested file:
      .../zephyr/cmake/app/boilerplate.cmake

The file was a compatibility shim that only forwarded to
find_package(Zephyr), which this CMakeLists.txt already calls on the line
before it, so the include is dropped and nothing else changes.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Yuichi Kusakabe <yuichi_kusakabe@jp.honda>
Upstream-Status: Pending [xen-troops/zephyr-dom0-xt]
---
diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 9a9e45f..1e4075e 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -5,8 +5,6 @@ cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.13.1)
 
 find_package(Zephyr REQUIRED HINTS $ENV{ZEPHYR_BASE})
 
-include($ENV{ZEPHYR_BASE}/cmake/app/boilerplate.cmake NO_POLICY_SCOPE)
-
 project(xen-dom0)
 
 include_directories(app PRIVATE ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include)
